   ("rainbow-book", "THE RAINBOW BOOK · RB1", "#9a7fd0", "educational · the format · five papers, one subject · 10", "THE RAINBOW BOOK (RB1) — David's STANDING FORMAT, set up so that when ROOT0 asks for a RAINBOW this is the deliverable: one subject rendered as FIVE papers, five angles, five colours, in order — WHITE the formal specification (definitions, element inventory, graph properties, normative claims with proofs; answers WHAT IT IS), GREEN the build (how to wire it, parts, checklist, use-cases, a working interactive; answers HOW YOU MAKE IT), PURPLE the reason (why the shape recurs, the same minimality re-derived across geometry/power/governance/consensus/verification; answers WHY IT MATTERS), BLUEPRINT the schematic (the literal drawing: netlist, node table, pinout, bill of elements, title block, revision; fab-ready), and VOID the synthesis (the four angles collapse back into the one object they were always angles ON — the home paper, dark). The worked example, embedded in all five: the THREE-BODY MESH — K₃, three bodies (A·B·C) fully bridged, 3 bridges, 6 ports, 9 elements, diameter 1, the minimum complete + fault-tolerant + SELF-WITNESSING network (two is a mirror; three triangulates; three is the smallest closed figure that can check itself without stepping outside — the triad of the J-junction closed into a ring). 10 emergents (the five paper-types + the rainbow format + the spectrum order + the worked example: the mesh / 9 elements / three-witnesses-itself). Builds on ROOT0's five Claude-in-Chrome papers, embedded; a five-band white→green→purple→blueprint→void spectrum with K₃ at centre; full .dlw. Educational."),
   ("anabasis", "ANABASIS · ANB", "#4fd6a8", "educational · agentic web dev · the front of the frontier · <• · 13", "ANABASIS (ANB) — ἀνάβασις, the going-up: an educational sphere on AGENTIC WEB DEVELOPMENT that SAVES THE METHOD — David's F/M/B (front/middle/back) topology rendered as a teachable RING on the J-junction <•. FRONT = the machine/cockpit + push origin; MIDDLE = the one public, witnessed, deterministic membrane (the <• crossing — an honest mirror, not a stage); BACK = the store (git) + the runner (the host). The laptop is the only DUAL node (front+back) that closes the ring. Thesis: tools are fungible (Docker/Railway/Fly.io rent the boxes this quarter), topology is not (the arrows git→build→serve→http survive them); and on the frontier the reader of your middle is an AGENT, not only a human — so serve it (deterministic endpoints, /.well-known, JSON feeds, schema). Cross-links the J-junction. 13 emergents (front/middle/back/ring/dual-node/witnessed-dot/honest-mirror/container/bridge/agent-reader/second-eye/anabasis); one-line ascent-into-<• glyph; full .dlw. Educational."),
