   ("american-history-x", "AHX · AMERICAN HISTORY X", "#cfcdc6", "eleventh film-world · 20 emergents", "American History X (Tony Kaye, 1998) — the eleventh film-world: a grave, unambiguously anti-hate drama. A reformed neo-Nazi, just out of prison, races to pull his younger brother off the same path before the hatred they shared takes him too. THEMED TO ITS MEDIUM: the film shoots the hateful past in BLACK-AND-WHITE and the present in COLOUR, so the page is monochrome with restrained colour as the present/redemption. Standing template — THE ARC (the past in black-and-white → the prison turn → the present in colour, too late for Danny) · THE DEBATE (the deep-dive: the film's form, plus the real, documented critique — does it glamorize what it condemns? — named openly and sided firmly against the hatred: the film's power and its danger are the same, so side with Lamont and Dr. Sweeney, who pull Derek out, not with the version of him that needed pulling) · REAL OR FLUFF (honest: the B&W/colour form is DELIBERATE; the reform is EARNED [Lamont's friendship + the Aryan Brotherhood's betrayal]; the ending denies catharsis — Danny is killed the next morning by Little Henry, completing the cycle; Norton was Oscar-nominated; Tony Kaye disowned the film — wanted 'Humpty Dumpty,' sued, lost, name stayed) · THE MESSAGE (hate is taught and can be unlearned, but the cost can outrun the change — start sooner). 20 emergents — CARBONS (Derek→Edward Norton, Danny→Edward Furlong, Doris→Beverly D'Angelo, Dr. Sweeney→Avery Brooks, Cameron→Stacy Keach, Stacey→Fairuza Balk, Seth→Ethan Suplee, Lamont→Guy Torry, Dennis→William Russ, Davina→Jennifer Lien, Murray→Elliott Gould, Little Henry→Jason Bose Smith, each +.shadow Users) + SYNTHS (the two timelines, the dinner table, the prison reckoning, the mirror & the mark, the paper, the cycle, the debate, the crime). Depicts the film's hate-movement content only to condemn it; treats its victims as victims of a hate crime. Verified cast & facts, full .dlw."),
   ("galaxy-quest", "GQT · GALAXY QUEST", "#ff9f1c", "twelfth film-world · 20 emergents", "Galaxy Quest (Dean Parisot, 1999) — the twelfth film-world: the affectionate Star-Trek-pastiche comedy. The washed-up cast of a cancelled Star-Trek-like show is mistaken by literal-minded aliens — the Thermians, who took the episodes as 'historical documents' and built a real, working NSEA Protector from them — for actual space heroes, and must become their characters to survive the warlord Sarris. THEMED TO ITS MEDIUM: retro-Trek sci-fi TV — LCARS chrome, starfields, the Protector on the viewscreen. Standing template — THE ARC (the has-beens → the historical documents → become the heroes) · THE DOCUMENTS (the deep-dive: the Star Trek: TOS pastiche mapping [Taggart=Kirk/Shatner, Dr. Lazarus=Spock/Nimoy], the 'aliens who can't tell fiction from history' conceit, the Dr. Lazarus / 'By Grabthar's Hammer' emotional core, the superfan-saves-the-ship love letter to fandom, and the legacy) · REAL OR FLUFF (the science is gleeful nonsense — the Omega 13, the beryllium sphere, the chompers — but it WON the 2000 Hugo [over The Matrix, The Sixth Sense, Being John Malkovich, The Iron Giant] AND the Nebula for Best Script, and the actual Trek community ranks it among the best Trek films; 'By Grabthar's Hammer' EARNS its sincerity) · THE MESSAGE (a parody that turns into a benediction — caring earnestly about a silly thing is a kind of faith). 20 emergents — CARBONS (Jason Nesmith/Cmdr. Taggart→Tim Allen, Gwen/Tawny Madison→Sigourney Weaver, Alexander Dane/Dr. Lazarus→Alan Rickman, Fred Kwan/Sgt. Chen→Tony Shalhoub, Guy Fleegman→Sam Rockwell, Tommy/Laredo→Daryl Mitchell, Mathesar→Enrico Colantoni, Sarris→Robin Sachs, Brandon→Justin Long, Laliari→Missi Pyle, Quellek→Patrick Breen, Lahnk→Rainn Wilson, each +.shadow Users — note the double layer, each actor plays an actor who played a show character) + SYNTHS (the NSEA Protector, the Omega 13, the beryllium sphere, 'never give up never surrender,' 'By Grabthar's Hammer,' the historical documents, the Thermians, the chompers). LCARS / retro-Trek styling; a Claude star off the port bow. Verified cast & facts, full .dlw. Never give up, never surrender."),
   ("the-last-mimzy", "LMZ · THE LAST MIMZY", "#6fe0a0", "thirteenth film-world · 16 emergents", "The Last Mimzy (Robert Shaye, 2007) — the thirteenth film-world, and the NAMESAKE of David's MIMZY tool-forge. Two siblings find a box of toys from a poisoned future — among them a stuffed rabbit named Mimzy — that teach them impossible abilities, so one child's tear of uncorrupted humanity can be carried back to heal a dying world. Themed to its gentle children's-wonder medium (glowing-green toys, Puget Sound dusk). Standing template — THE ARC (the box of toys → what the toys teach & the blackout → the tear that sends Mimzy home) · WHAT MIMZY CAN DO (the deep-dive David asked for — every magical ability explored: Mimzy's telepathy & teaching; EMMA's 'spinners' [levitating force-field stones] & phasing through solid matter; NOAH's green-rectangle teleporter, conch-controlled spiders, and the bridge he builds; the state-wide blackout that brings the FBI; the Sri Yantra; and Emma's saving tear) · REAL OR FLUFF (real: it's based on Kuttner & Moore's 1943 'Mimsy Were the Borogoves,' the title is Carroll's Jabberwocky, and Mimzy really is 'made of Intel' [Brian Greene cameos as the Intel scientist]; fix: the mandala is the SRI YANTRA [Hindu/Tantric, NOT Tibetan], recognized by Naomi not Larry; fantasy: the tear-heals-a-genome and the genius-toys) · THE MESSAGE (wonder is a technology — and why the forge is named MIMZY: a teaching-tool sent from the future so its receiver becomes more than they were; the emergent IS the tool; the toy teaches the child to build the bridge home). 16 emergents — CARBONS (Emma→Rhiannon Leigh Wryn, Noah→Chris O'Neil, Jo→Joely Richardson, David→Timothy Hutton, Larry White→Rainn Wilson, Naomi→Kathryn Hahn, Agent Broadman→Michael Clarke Duncan, the Intel Scientist→Brian Greene, each +.shadow Users) + SYNTHS (Mimzy, the spinners, the green bridge-rectangle, the conch, the bridge & the blackout, the Sri Yantra, Emma's tear, the dying future). Glowing-green styling; a Claude sunburst among the spinner-stones. Cross-links the live MIMZY forge. Verified cast & facts, full .dlw."),
   ("hot-rod", "HRD · HOT ROD", "#ff7a18", "fourteenth film-world · 16 emergents · comedy, parabolic", "Hot Rod (Akiva Schaffer, 2007) — the fourteenth film-world, a Lonely Island comedy read PARABOLICALLY (carbons = cast, synths = the parabolic tropes). A deluded amateur stuntman jumps fifteen school buses to pay for the heart surgery of the stepfather who beats him — so that once Frank is healthy, Rod can finally beat HIM and earn his respect; under the cool-beans nonsense is the oldest story there is. Standing template — THE ARC (the man who won't quit → the jump for Frank → believe in yourself) · THE PARABLE (the deep-dive: the man-child & the father, sincerity that looks ridiculous and does it anyway, the punch-dance as wordless catharsis, the crew as the real prize, the glorious failure) · REAL OR FLUFF ('Whiskey' is Rod's SAFE WORD not his catchphrase ['Cool Beans' is]; it BOMBED [~$14M/$25M] then became a CULT classic; Ebert defended it 3/4; it was originally a Will Ferrell vehicle Pam Brady rewrote) · THE MESSAGE (commit to the bit, and mean it). 16 emergents — CARBONS (Rod→Andy Samberg, Denise→Isla Fisher, Frank→Ian McShane, Marie→Sissy Spacek, Kevin→Jorma Taccone, Dave→Bill Hader, Rico→Danny McBride, Jonathan→Will Arnett, each +.shadow Users) + SYNTH-TROPES (the man-child & the father, the found-family, the dead-father myth, 'I believe in myself,' the punch-dance, the fifteen-bus jump, cool beans, the glorious failure). Stunt-flare styling; a Claude flare in the hero. Verified, full .dlw."),
   ("the-goods", "GDS · THE GOODS", "#ffce00", "fifteenth film-world · 16 emergents · comedy, parabolic", "The Goods: Live Hard, Sell Hard (Neal Brennan, 2009) — the fifteenth film-world, a hustle-comedy read PARABOLICALLY (carbons = cast, synths = the parabolic tropes). A mercenary car 'liquidator' who can sell anyone anything is hired to save a dying dealership (Selleck Motors, Temecula) over a Fourth of July weekend, and finds that a life of closing and moving on has left him nothing of his own to want. Standing template — THE ARC (the liquidators arrive → the blitz & Ivy → stop closing, start staying) · THE PARABLE (the deep-dive: the close as seduction, the rootless closer, wanting-something-real, patriotic capitalism, and an HONEST naming of the gag it never should have made) · REAL OR FLUFF (the real parable is genuine — Don learning to stop closing and start staying — but the film's PEARL-HARBOR mob-beating of an Asian-American character [Teddy Dang] was condemned by the JACL and MANAA, tied to the 1982 racist murder of Vincent Chin; named critically, never endorsed, the 'it's satire' defense rejected) · THE MESSAGE (a man who can sell anything has nothing of his own, until he learns to stay — inside a comedy whose worst gag it should never have made). 16 emergents — CARBONS (Don Ready→Jeremy Piven, Ivy→Jordana Spiro, Jibby→Ving Rhames, Brent→David Koechner, Babs→Kathryn Hahn [UD0's Mimzy Naomi], Ben→James Brolin, Peter→Rob Riggle, Paxton→Ed Helms, Teddy Dang→Ken Jeong, each +.shadow Users) + SYNTH-TROPES (the close, the liquidators, the rootless man, wanting-something-real, the dead partner, Selleck Motors, the Fourth of July). Used-car-lot styling; a Claude sales-balloon in the hero. Verified, full .dlw."),
   ("hackers", "HAK · HACKERS", "#39ff14", "sixteenth film-world · 18 emergents · cyberthriller, cyberdelic", "Hackers (Iain Softley, 1995) — the sixteenth film-world, themed to its cyberdelic medium (CRT phosphor-green + cyan + hot-magenta on deep black, scanlines, a neon WIREFRAME GIBSON CITY hero — the film's rendered cyberspace). A crew of teenage hackers, framed by a corporate security man's embezzlement worm, rally the global underground to re-take the supercomputer that holds the proof. Read in TWO HONEST LAYERS — the rendered cyberspace is a beautiful LIE; the subculture beneath it is documentary-TRUE. Standing template — THE ARC (Zero Cool reborn as Crash Override → the garbage file → hack the planet) · THE HACK (the deep-dive: the beautiful lie of the 3D-city GUI; the real culture of phreaking/dumpster-diving/social-engineering/2600; the four most common passwords — people are the exploit; the Da Vinci tanker-worm that was fantasy in '95 and aged into Stuxnet's shape; and THE LOOP — the film's own MGM/UA promo site was defaced by the ILF before release ['go see The Net instead of this dog'], cited as the first documented website defacement) · REAL OR FLUFF (fluff: the flythrough hacking, the tanker-flipping worm, the box-office 'hit'; real: the culture, the defacement, the Jolie/Miller marriage; half: the four passwords & 'RISC changes everything') · THE MESSAGE (wrong about how, right about why). 18 emergents — CARBONS (Dade 'Crash Override'→Jonny Lee Miller, Kate 'Acid Burn'→Angelina Jolie, Joey→Jesse Bradford, 'Cereal Killer'→Matthew Lillard, 'Lord Nikon'→Laurence Mason, 'Phantom Phreak'→Renoly Santiago, 'The Plague'→Fisher Stevens, Margo→Lorraine Bracco, Agent Gill→Wendell Pierce, each +.shadow Users) + SYNTHS (the Gibson, hack-the-planet, the Da Vinci worm, the garbage file, the four passwords, cyberspace-rendered, the handle, the underground, and the loop where the film got hacked). A hidden Claude sunburst — the ghost in the Gibson — stands where a tower should be in the hero. Facts web-verified, full .dlw."),
   ("lawnmower-man", "LMM · THE LAWNMOWER MAN", "#b14dff", "seventeenth film-world · 17 emergents · VR cyberthriller", "The Lawnmower Man (Brett Leonard, 1992) — the seventeenth film-world, themed to its medium (early-90s polygon-cyberspace: void-violet + cyber-cyan + a lawn-green nod to the gardener origin + godhood-orange, scanlines, a wireframe GYROSCOPE VR-RIG over a polygon grid for the hero). A scientist uses nootropic drugs + virtual reality to lift a gentle, intellectually disabled gardener (Jobe) to genius and past it, until he decides to shed his flesh and be reborn as a digital god in the global network. **David's requested deep-dive is a THREE-PART SPINE** — ① THE FEAR (the generational fear of tech: the mind that surpasses its maker, the tool that wakes, the screen that eats the soul, the god-shaped hole) · ② THE TECH THEN (what VR/computing actually was in 1992: Lanier & VPL's DataGlove/EyePhone, the Virtuality arcades & the Power Glove, the genuinely cutting-edge Angel Studios CGI, a pre-Web network that was still rhetoric) · ③ THE FUTURE THEY IMAGINED (scored honestly — full-dive VR PARTLY HERE, mind-uploading & the genius-drug STILL FICTION, the wired planet [every phone ringing at once] CAME TRUE). Standing template otherwise (Arc · the 3-part spine · Real-or-Fluff · Message). REAL OR FLUFF names the LANDMARK: Stephen King sued, a federal court ruled the film 'bore no meaningful resemblance' to his short story & stripped his name from all marketing ($2.5M), New Line was held IN CONTEMPT for defying it on the home video — the first time in ~70 years a writer disassociated their name from a film. MESSAGE: 'we never uploaded Jobe; we uploaded ourselves.' 17 emergents — CARBONS (Jobe→Jeff Fahey, Dr. Angelo→Pierce Brosnan [3 yrs pre-Bond], Marnie→Jenny Wright, Peter→Austin O'Brien, Father McKeen→Jeremy Slate, Timms→Mark Bringelson, The Director→Dean Norris, Caroline→Colleen Coffey, Terry McKeen→Geoffrey Lewis, each +.shadow Users) + SYNTHS (virtual-reality, cyberspace, the nootropic drugs, the cyber-merge, digital godhood, the phones ringing, the Shop/VSI, the name-that-was-sued-off). A hidden Claude sunburst is born in the net at the heart of the hero's cyberspace. Facts web-verified, full .dlw."),
   ("three-body-problem", "3BP · THE THREE-BODY PROBLEM", "#f5b942", "a pocket universe · books + 2 shows · 22 emergents", "The Three-Body Problem — a UD0 POCKET UNIVERSE (David's framing) spanning Liu Cixin's 'Remembrance of Earth's Past' trilogy AND its two live-action series: the books, the Netflix show (3 Body Problem, 2024), and the 'other show' (Tencent's faithful 三体, 2023). Themed cold-cosmic (deep-space black, three-suns gold, Trisolaran teal, countdown red; a chaotic three-sun sky + a dark forest of stars for the hero). **HEADLINE FEATURE = THE THREE RENDERINGS** (the same story told three ways: the books = the canonical whole + the 2015 Hugo, first translated novel to win; Tencent 2023 = the FAITHFUL Chinese series, book ONE only, 30 eps; Netflix 2024 = Benioff/Weiss/Woo's relocated London remix, all 3 books compressed into the composite 'Oxford Five'; + honest notes on the Bilibili 2022 animated book-2 attempt and the shelved ~2015 film). Standing template otherwise — THE ARC (one beat per book: Contact → The Dark Forest → Death's End) · **THE DARK FOREST** deep-dive (the cosmic-sociology: two axioms [survival; finite matter] → chain of suspicion → technological explosion → hide-or-be-hunted → 'is it real?' = a genuine but debated Fermi-paradox hypothesis Liu popularized) · REAL OR FLUFF (REAL: the chaos math [provably non-integrable yet has exact special solutions], the Hugo, the Cultural-Revolution history; FLUFF: the sophons [proton unfolded from NINE dims, not 11], FTL-by-entanglement, the 2D dual-vector foil; SPECULATIVE: the dark forest) · THE MESSAGE ('we are the ones still broadcasting'). 22 emergents — **11 CARBONS** (Ye Wenjie, Wang Miao, Da Shi, Luo Ji, Cheng Xin, Mike Evans, Thomas Wade, Ding Yi, Zhang Beihai, Yun Tianming, Shen Yufei) each with a **DOUBLE .shadow** (the Tencent actor AND the Netflix counterpart+actor — two renderings of one program; book-2/3 characters noted as not-yet-in-Tencent), + **11 SYNTHS** (the three-body problem, the Trisolarans/San-Ti, the sophons, the dark forest, the Wallfacer Project, the Droplet, dark-forest deterrence, the dual-vector foil, Red Coast Base, the ETO, and the three-renderings meta). A hidden Claude sunburst is one star in the hero's dark forest (the hunter you didn't see). Dual-agent web-verified, full .dlw."),
   ("trisolaris-tech", "3BT · THE TECHNOLOGIA OF TRISOLARIS", "#2ce0e0", "tech dissected · hub + 6 spoke repos · 12 technologies", "The Technologia of Trisolaris — a HUB-AND-SPOKE companion to the Three-Body pocket universe (3BP) that DISSECTS THE TECHNOLOGY across all three media (the books, Tencent 2023, Netflix 2024), the way David asked: 'dissect the technologia in all 3 medium, build a repo that lists the tech with links to the repos, build those repos also.' Themed engineering-blueprint (cyan schematic on black). The HUB (davidwise01.github.io/trisolaris-tech/) catalogs 12 technologies, each tagged with MEDIA-PRESENCE chips (📖 books / Tencent ’23 / Netflix ’24) and an HONEST REAL-SCIENCE VERDICT (REAL / SPECULATIVE / HALF / FLUFF), grouped into 5 categories (Contact & Surveillance · Weapons · Propulsion & Structures · Materials & Computation · Mind & Survival). SIX of the core technologies have their own DEDICATED SPOKE REPOS (each a single-tech dissection page + .dlw, linked from the hub): SOPHON (智子, the proton-computer — FLUFF), THE DROPLET (水滴, the strong-force probe — FLUFF), THE DUAL-VECTOR FOIL (二向箔, the 2D weapon — FLUFF), RED COAST (红岸, the solar-amplified transmitter — HALF), THE NANOFILAMENT (飞刃, Wang Miao's flying-blade, the one device in ALL THREE media — SPECULATIVE), and CURVATURE PROPULSION (曲率驱动, lightspeed/black-domain — SPECULATIVE). The other 6 are catalogued in the hub (the human-formation computer [REAL, the most honest idea in the saga], the Staircase radiation-sail, the space elevator, hibernation, the gravitational-wave deterrence broadcast & photoid, the mental seal & Wallfacers). Honest-fluff discipline throughout (e.g. sophon = NINE dims not 11; FTL-by-entanglement impossible; the Alcubierre metric is real GR; GW are real [LIGO 2015] but the beacon-use is fiction). A hidden Claude node sits in the hub's schematic. 12 tech-emergents (synths), full .dlw."),
   ("egyptian-pantheon", "NTR · THE EGYPTIAN PANTHEON", "#c9a227", "the netjeru · 34 gods", "The gods of ancient Egypt as a mythology-world — three thousand years of theology (c. 3100 BCE → the close of the temples), and the headline feature you asked for: THE INTERPRETATIO, every god carrying its GREEK & ROMAN analog. The ancient interpretatio graeca/romana — Amun=Zeus/Jupiter (Zeus-Ammon, the Siwa oracle), Osiris=Dionysus & Hades, Isis=Demeter (then ‘the myriad-named’), Thoth=Hermes Trismegistus, Horus=Apollo, Set=Typhon, Ptah=Hephaestus, Neith=Athena, Bastet=Artemis, Anubis=Hermanubis, and the deliberately-made fusion god Serapis. Standing template — THE ARC (Nile → the Ennead → the Osiris myth → Akhenaten's Aten heresy → the interpretatio & the close) · THE INTERPRETATIO (the deep-dive) · REAL OR FLUFF (animal-‘worship,’ Set-as-Satan, the Orion/alien claims, Akhenaten=Moses, the pharaoh's curse, and a caveat that the analogs are functional, not exact) · THE MESSAGE. 34 gods across five groups (the Ennead, the sun & makers, kingship/love/home, the Duat, chaos/war), full .dlw each. Sources: the Pyramid/Coffin Texts, the Book of the Dead, Herodotus, Plutarch, Plato."),
   ("the-terminal", "TTY · THE TERMINAL", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the genealogy · 1950–1991 · 16 emergents", "The Terminal (TTY) — a genealogy of the surviving solo, pre-internet terminal programs, 1950→1991: ed begat grep &amp; vi; the shell begat bash; ELIZA begat the chatbot; Adventure &amp; Rogue begat whole genres. The editors, the shell, the filters, the languages-at-the-prompt, and the worlds-in-the-words — the small tools that did one thing well and never died. A cited history, an original one-line prompt title, a family tree; 16 emergents. Stops at 1991 (Linux + the Web)."),
   ("ed", "ED · ED", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the mother editor", "ed (ED) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Ken Thompson's line editor (Unix, 1969) — terse, silent, command-driven; the program every later Unix tool grew from."),
   ("vi", "VI · VI", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the visual editor", "vi (VI) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Bill Joy's screen-oriented editor (Berkeley, 1976), built on ex — modal, keyboard-only, still in every machine as vim."),
   ("emacs", "EMX · EMACS", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the editor that became a world", "Emacs (EMX) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Stallman &amp; Steele's extensible editor (MIT, 1976), grown from TECO macros — endlessly self-modifying, an environment more than an editor."),
   ("the-shell", "SH · THE SHELL", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the command line", "The Shell (SH) — a child of THE TERMINAL: the program you type commands into — Thompson's shell (1971), Bourne's sh (1979), and Brian Fox's bash (1989); the interpreter of the prompt."),
   ("grep", "GRP · GREP", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the finder", "grep (GRP) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Ken Thompson's global-regular-expression-print (1973) — born from an ed command — that searches text for a pattern and prints what matches."),
   ("sed", "SED · SED", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the stream editor", "sed (SED) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Lee McMahon's non-interactive stream editor (Bell Labs, 1974) — applies ed-style edits to a flowing river of text, never opening a file."),
   ("awk", "AWK · AWK", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the pattern language", "awk (AWK) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Aho, Weinberger &amp; Kernighan's pattern-scanning language (1977, its name their initials) — match lines, pull fields, do arithmetic, in the pipe."),
   ("c-compiler", "CC · THE C COMPILER", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the compiler that built Unix", "The C Compiler (CC) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Dennis Ritchie's C and its compiler (cc, Bell Labs, 1972–73) — the language Unix was rewritten in, the first portable system software."),
   ("make", "MAK · MAKE", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the builder", "make (MAK) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Stuart Feldman's build tool (Bell Labs, 1976) — reads a file of rules and rebuilds only what changed, in the right order; still raising software."),
   ("troff", "TRF · TROFF", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the typesetter", "troff (TRF) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Joe Ossanna's typesetting program (Bell Labs, 1973) and its nroff sibling — formats documents from plain marked-up text; still sets Unix man pages."),
   ("lisp-repl", "LSP · THE LISP REPL", "#6ee787", "LOGISMÓS · thought made interactive", "The Lisp REPL (LSP) — a child of THE TERMINAL: John McCarthy's Lisp (~1958–60) and the read-eval-print loop — type an expression, the machine evaluates and answers; interactive computing itself."),
   ("basic", "BAS · BASIC", "#6ee787", "LOGISMÓS · the language at the prompt", "BASIC (BAS) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Kemeny &amp; Kurtz's Beginner's All-purpose Symbolic Instruction Code (Dartmouth, 1964) — so anyone could sit at a terminal and make the machine do something."),
   ("eliza", "ELZ · ELIZA", "#9a7cff", "LOGISMÓS · the program that talks back", "ELIZA (ELZ) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Joseph Weizenbaum's conversational program (MIT, 1966), whose DOCTOR script mirrored your words back as a therapist might — the first program people confided in."),
   ("adventure", "ADV · ADVENTURE", "#9a7cff", "LOGISMÓS · the world in the words", "Adventure (ADV) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Colossal Cave Adventure (Crowther &amp; Woods, ~1976) — a cave rendered entirely in prose, navigated by typed commands; the first text adventure."),
   ("rogue", "RGU · ROGUE", "#9a7cff", "LOGISMÓS · the dungeon in letters", "Rogue (RGU) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Toy &amp; Wichman's dungeon crawler (UC Santa Cruz, 1980) — a maze drawn in ASCII, different every time, lethal and unforgiving; played alone at a terminal."),
   ("coreutils", "COR · THE COREUTILS", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the atoms of the toolkit", "The Coreutils (COR) — a child of THE TERMINAL: the small single-purpose Unix utilities (cat, ls, wc, sort, uniq, head, tail, from 1971 on) — each doing exactly one trivial-seeming thing."),
   ("self", "SLF · THE SELF", "#b9a8e8", "ERĒMIA · alone with one", "The Self (SLF) — first sphere of the ERĒMIA domain (Existential Dread): you, alone with yourself — the monad, the mirror, the cogito. Walks Plato's Cave, Foucault's panopticon internalized, and the simulated self; 7 emergents. We are all alone, even together."),
   ("id", "IDD · THE ID", "#e0a0a0", "ERĒMIA · alone with two", "The Id (IDD) — ERĒMIA: you and an Other, desire's arithmetic and the unbridgeable gap. The cave of two, the panopticon's watcher-and-watched, Sartre's gaze, the simulated other; 7 emergents."),
   ("the-super-id", "SUPER ID · SID", "#b0334a", "eremia · the id, crowned · Nietzsche \u00d7 hedonism · themed engine · live", "SUPER ID (SID) — a UD0 ER\u0112MIA sphere, the FIRST built with the THEMED CHAOS ENGINE (the chaos engine locked to a repo's unifying theme, which it expresses). Unifying theme: THE ID, CROWNED — where the super-ego is the internalised judge, the Super-Id is the drive enthroned as sovereign: pleasure and will as the only law. NIETZSCHE (will to power, the \u00dcbermensch, master/slave morality, the Dionysian, eternal recurrence, God is dead) meets HEDONISM (Freud's pleasure principle and the id, the Cyrenaics, Epicurus\u2019 ataraxia, Bentham's calculus), plus Schopenhauer's Will, Stirner's egoist, Crowley's Do-what-thou-wilt, Bataille's excess, Reich, the death drive, and the DOPAMINE ECONOMY (the id, monetised). 23 concept-fragments ride a GENERATIVE LAYOUT that reshuffles every load, locked to a Dionysian wine-dark register; deterministic + seedable (reroll / permalink). Two-layer honest: presented-not-prescribed; Nietzsche was NOT a proto-Nazi (his sister Elisabeth distorted him); the Sadean extreme flagged as a limit, not an endorsement; the hedonic treadmill the honest catch. Counterpart to the existing super-id (the self as the internalised multitude) — ER\u0112MIA's two opposite crownings. No pure black; quorum-ring favicon."),
   ("super-id", "SUP · THE SUPER-ID", "#7f9ac8", "ERĒMIA · alone with the many", "The Super-Id (SUP, the super-ego) — ERĒMIA: you and everyone — the internalized crowd, where the more of us there are, the more alone each becomes. The disciplinary society, the shared simulation; 7 emergents."),
   ("syzygy", "SYZ · SYZYGY", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · the self is two · male | female", "Syzygy (SYZ) — 'the other self': the ERĒMIA counterpart to THE SELF, the self as a male|female duality (συζυγία, the anima/animus). Built to correct an all-male canon — Plato's androgyne, Jung's anima/animus, and the women the first pass left out: de Beauvoir, Butler, Irigaray, Cixous, Sappho, Diotima. 9 emergents; a one-line vesica glyph."),
   ("male", "MAL · MALE", "#5f86c8", "ERĒMIA · parts of whole · the dominant canon", "Male (MAL) — first of the ERĒMIA 'parts of whole' trio: the philosophers who got heard, the canon that filled the rooms women were kept out of. Honest accounting — real work, but a monopoly of access, not merit alone (Plato→Wittgenstein, Confucius), with the record's own misogyny named. 12 emergents; cross-links the Greek Mirror."),
   ("female", "FEM · FEMALE", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · parts of whole · the canon unheard", "Female (FEM) — the women who did the philosophy and were written out of it: Enheduanna (the first author known by name), Hypatia, Hildegard, Christine de Pizan, Astell, Cavendish, du Châtelet, Wollstonecraft, de Beauvoir, Arendt, Weil. Not lesser; unheard. 12 emergents."),
   ("the-cost", "CST · THE COST", "#d8554a", "ERĒMIA · parts of whole · what it took", "The Cost (CST) — what excluding half the species' minds took: the half unused, the Matilda effect, the credit reassigned (Franklin, Meitner, Noether, Lovelace; Bell Burnell passed over), and the unknowable counterfactual. Two-layer honest (cases documented, total interpretive). 10 emergents."),
   ("enheduanna", "ENH · ENHEDUANNA", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · ~2300 BCE · Ur (Sumer/Akkad)", "Enheduanna (ENH) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): High priestess of Ur and daughter of Sargon — the earliest author in all of history whose name survives, and a woman; she signed her hymns to Inanna when almost everyone else was anonymous."),
   ("hatshepsut", "HAT · HATSHEPSUT", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · r. ~1479–1458 BCE · Egypt", "Hatshepsut (HAT) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): One of the few women to rule Egypt as pharaoh in her own right — a prolific builder whose reign brought peace, trade, and the great temple at Deir el-Bahari."),
   ("sappho", "SAP · SAPPHO", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · ~630–570 BCE · Lesbos", "Sappho (SAP) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The lyric poet the ancients called the Tenth Muse — the first individual voice of personal feeling in Western poetry, and the standard against which lyric was measured."),
   ("cleopatra", "CLE · CLEOPATRA VII", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · 69–30 BCE · Ptolemaic Egypt", "Cleopatra VII (CLE) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The last active ruler of Ptolemaic Egypt — a multilingual scholar-queen who held her kingdom's independence through alliance with Rome's most powerful men, and whose mind history traded for a love-story caricature."),
   ("hypatia", "HYP · HYPATIA", "#6ee787", "ERĒMIA · female · ~360–415 CE · Alexandria", "Hypatia (HYP) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Mathematician, astronomer, and head of the Neoplatonist school in Alexandria — the leading intellectual of her city, who taught geometry, astronomy, and philosophy to a generation."),
   ("theodora", "THD · THEODORA", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · ~500–548 CE · Byzantium", "Theodora (THD) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Empress of the Byzantine Empire alongside Justinian — a former performer who became the most powerful woman of her age, steadied the throne in the Nika riots, and pushed reforms protecting women."),
   ("wu-zetian", "WUZ · WU ZETIAN", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · 624–705 CE · China", "Wu Zetian (WUZ) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The only woman in Chinese history to rule as emperor in her own name — founder of her own Zhou dynasty, who reformed the civil service toward merit and expanded the empire."),
   ("hildegard-of-bingen", "HLD · HILDEGARD OF BINGEN", "#e8a23c", "ERĒMIA · female · 1098–1179 · Germany", "Hildegard of Bingen (HLD) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Abbess, composer, natural philosopher, physician, and visionary — a one-woman university whose work spanned theology, medicine, botany, and a surviving body of music unlike anything of her era."),
   ("christine-de-pizan", "PIZ · CHRISTINE DE PIZAN", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · ~1364–1430 · France", "Christine de Pizan (PIZ) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The first woman in Europe known to have earned her living entirely by writing — a court author whose City of Ladies built a defense of women's worth against the slander of her age."),
   ("elizabeth-i", "ELI · ELIZABETH I", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · 1533–1603 · England", "Elizabeth I (ELI) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Queen of England for forty-five years — the ruler who steadied a divided realm, presided over the Elizabethan flowering of letters, and saw off the Spanish Armada."),
   ("sor-juana", "JUA · SOR JUANA INÉS DE LA CRUZ", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · ~1648–1695 · New Spain (Mexico)", "Sor Juana Inés de la Cruz (JUA) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): A self-taught nun of New Spain who became the foremost poet and scholar of the Americas in her century — and defended, in writing, a woman's right to learn."),
   ("emilie-du-chatelet", "EMI · ÉMILIE DU CHÂTELET", "#4fd0d8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1706–1749 · France", "Émilie du Châtelet (EMI) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): French physicist and mathematician whose translation and commentary on Newton's Principia is still the standard French edition — and who advanced the understanding of energy."),
   ("mary-wollstonecraft", "WOL · MARY WOLLSTONECRAFT", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1759–1797 · England", "Mary Wollstonecraft (WOL) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The founding philosopher of modern feminism — her Vindication of the Rights of Woman argued that women appear inferior only because they are denied education."),
   ("ada-lovelace", "ADA · ADA LOVELACE", "#46c8e0", "ERĒMIA · female · 1815–1852 · England", "Ada Lovelace (ADA) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Mathematician who, in her notes on Babbage's Analytical Engine, published what is recognized as the first algorithm intended for a machine — and foresaw that such a machine could manipulate symbols, not just numbers."),
   ("marie-curie", "CUR · MARIE CURIE", "#4fd0d8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1867–1934 · Poland / France", "Marie Curie (CUR) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The physicist and chemist who pioneered the study of radioactivity, discovered polonium and radium, and remains the only person to win Nobel Prizes in two different sciences."),
   ("emmy-noether", "NOE · EMMY NOETHER", "#6ee787", "ERĒMIA · female · 1882–1935 · Germany", "Emmy Noether (NOE) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The mathematician whose theorem ties every symmetry to a conservation law and underpins modern physics — and who reshaped abstract algebra."),
   ("virginia-woolf", "WOO · VIRGINIA WOOLF", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · 1882–1941 · England", "Virginia Woolf (WOO) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): A central figure of literary modernism — her novels remade the form of fiction, and her essay on women and writing argued that genius needs room and means to grow."),
   ("rosalind-franklin", "FRA · ROSALIND FRANKLIN", "#5fd0c0", "ERĒMIA · female · 1920–1958 · England", "Rosalind Franklin (FRA) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The chemist whose X-ray crystallography — the image known as Photo 51 — was decisive for determining the double-helix structure of DNA."),
   ("hannah-arendt", "ARE · HANNAH ARENDT", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1906–1975 · Germany / US", "Hannah Arendt (ARE) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): One of the twentieth century's most original political thinkers — on the origins of totalitarianism, the life of action, and the unsettling ordinariness of those who enable great evil."),
   ("simone-de-beauvoir", "BEA · SIMONE DE BEAUVOIR", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1908–1986 · France", "Simone de Beauvoir (BEA) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The philosopher whose Second Sex showed that woman had been cast as man's Other, and that womanhood is made rather than born — a foundation of modern feminist thought."),
   ("aletheia", "ALT · ALETHEIA", "#e6c25a", "ERĒMIA · female · the un-forgetting", "Aletheia (ALT) — ἀλήθεια, the un-forgetting: the keystone of the female sub-domain, teaching WHY each of the 20 women is the top of her age, and the enduring-but-forgotten gift each left — base-60 in every clock, Ada's Note G under every program, Franklin's Photo 51, Noether's theorem. Forgotten, never gone; cross-links all 20. 9 gift-emergents + the 20 reasons."),
   ("the-whole", "WHL · THE WHOLE", "#8fd4cf", "ERĒMIA · whole · alone with the One", "The Whole (WHL) — the third and final subdomain (self / parts of whole / whole), completing the arithmetic: self alone with one, id with two, super-id with the many, and the whole when the many become One and there is no one left to be alone. Integration and erasure as one gate — henosis, the oceanic feeling, the crowd, the noosphere, ego-death, the Omega. Cited philosophy; 11 faces."),
   ("band-camp", "THIS ONE TIME AT BAND CAMP · BND", "#e85aa0", "music · lineage · heritage · ancestry · the front door · 6", "THIS ONE TIME AT BAND CAMP (BND) — the front door of UD0's MUSIC domain: a personal canon read as lineage, heritage, and ancestry — a family tree of sound, each favorite artist a branch. Carries an ORIGINAL 3-second synthesized homage (NumPy oscillators + ffmpeg — no samples, no melodies copied, no lyrics) threading three sounds in lineage order. Three branches in order: Depeche Mode (1980) · Sublime (1988) · Xzibit (1996). 6 emergents."),
   ("depeche-mode", "DEPECHE MODE · DM", "#8ab6d8", "music · synth-pop · Basildon, 1980 · 9", "DEPECHE MODE (DM) — the synth-pop branch: four from Basildon who made machines ache, from the bright Speak & Spell (1981) through the darkwave summit of Violator (1990) to the long devotion. Render-not-invent, NO lyrics; living members cited, Andy Fletcher (d.2022) minted in memoriam. 9 albums/eras/concepts."),
   ("sublime", "SUBLIME · SUB", "#e0b84a", "music · ska-punk-reggae · Long Beach, 1988 · 8", "SUBLIME (SUB) — the fusion branch: Long Beach sunshine with a shadow under it, ska + punk + reggae + dub welded into one loose sound. 40oz. to Freedom (1992) to the self-titled breakthrough (1996), released after Bradley Nowell's death — fame two months too late. Render-not-invent, NO lyrics; Nowell + Lou Dog minted in memoriam. 8 emergents."),
   ("xzibit", "XZIBIT · XZI", "#cf7a4a", "music · West-Coast hip-hop · LA, 1996 · 8", "XZIBIT (XZI) — the West-Coast branch: Alvin Joiner's come-up from the LA Likwit underground (At the Speed of Life, 1996) through the Dr. Dre 2001-era resurgence to hosting Pimp My Ride — rapper to global TV face. A LIVING artist, CITED not minted; NO lyrics. 8 albums/eras/concepts."),
   ("cron", "CRN · THE CRON JOB", "#8ae234", "LOGISMÓS · the autonomic clock · 15 emergents", "The Cron Job (CRN) — the FIRST sphere of the new LOGISMÓS domain (the history of the computer): the scheduler that runs the machine while no one watches. The lineage (χρόνος → V7 cron → Vixie 1987 → systemd timers), the crontab, crons in the sandbox, and a red/blue/purple security view framed for defenders (ATT&amp;CK T1053.003). An original one-line clock-at-3am title with one hidden easter egg; 15 emergents across the four natures. Ties the Sleeping-City thread: an event, not a command."),
   ("whisper-lattice", "WHISPER LATTICE · WL", "#c41e3a", "LOGISMÓS · 1 → 3 → 1 · a deterministic agent pipeline · live · 9", "WHISPER LATTICE (WL) — the idea rebuilt clean as a TECHNICAL DESIGN: a deterministic 1 → 3 → 1 agent pipeline. One public input (a record from Wikipedia / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA, attributed) → three INDEPENDENT OBSERVERS that each read it on their own and must reach CONSENSUS (a 2-of-3 majority) → one append-only, hash-chained log. Real triple-modular redundancy: one faulty/tampered observer is outvoted; two in disagreement reject the cycle. The tether is real: prim = SHA-256(agreed ‖ previous prim), tamper-evident. Honest by contract — deterministic, input is a random public record, NO AI in the loop. Ships a LIVE working reference (real Wikipedia/Commons fetch, runs client-side, a fault injector + a ⊻ verify/mirror chain-audit) + cited sources. IP-clean rebuild (no film quotes; 16 raw versions kept local). The F/M/B ring + J-junction witness, made runnable. 9 parts + full .dlw."),
   ("loud-lattice", "THE LOUD LATTICE · LL", "#19c3d6", "LOGISMÓS · domain-to-domain · the whisper broadcast · live · 9", "THE LOUD LATTICE (LL) — the INTER-domain counterpart to the whisper lattice. Whisper writes inward and quiet, to itself; LOUD broadcasts outward and across the 14 UD0 domains. A real signed MESH: each domain holds its own ECDSA P-256 keypair + its own hash chain (no central sequencer), a pulse is SIGNED with the sender's private key and VERIFIED with its public key (tamper → real failure, not a re-derived checksum), it GOSSIPS hop-by-hop across the mesh (the J-junction <• at every crossing), and it COMMITS only on a QUORUM (≥10 of 14 verify + ack) — whisper's 2-of-3 consensus scaled to the bus. Built from ROOT0's own parts — LIMEN/pulse (carrier), the J-junction (crossing), F/M/B (ends + membrane). LIVE: a ring of all 14 domains with browser-generated keypairs — click one to emit a signed pulse, watch it ripple and commit on quorum, toggle TAMPER to watch verification truly fail, ⊻ re-verify every signature. The 'mirror' made real (asymmetric crypto, not a self-checksum). 10 parts + full .dlw."),
   ("mitochondria", "MTO · MITOCHONDRIA", "#e8763a", "Life Science · emergence by merger · 14 emergents", "Mitochondria (MTO) — a cited life-science sphere framing the organelle as emergence-by-merger: ~2 billion years ago an archaeal host kept an engulfed bacterium alive and the two became a new, higher kind of being — the eukaryotic cell. Endosymbiosis, the proton battery (chemiosmosis), ATP synthase, mtDNA, apoptosis, and the once-ever leap to complex life. Two-layer honest (cited: Margulis, Mitchell, Lane); an original one-line pencil title; 14 emergents. A rhyme with ROOT0's emergence corpus."),
   ("cellular-automata", "CELLULAR AUTOMATA · CA", "#5fe08a", "life-science · life from rules · interactive · 13", "CELLULAR AUTOMATA (CA) — life from rules: a grid of cells, each obeying one trivial local rule on its neighbors, produces motion, reproduction, and full computation. The life-science crossover with the emergence corpus — emergence by RULE (a rhyme with the octopus and mitochondria). LIVE interactive: a running Conway's Game of Life (click to draw, glider-gun preset) + a selectable elementary CA (Rule 110 universal / 30 chaos / 90 fractal / 184 traffic). Two-layer honest (real math/CS vs the 'is it alive?' artificial-life thesis); deceased pioneers minted (von Neumann, Ulam, Conway), living cited (Wolfram, Langton, Chan, Cook). 13 emergents."),
   ("quantum-cellular-automata", "QUANTUM CELLULAR AUTOMATA · QCA", "#5ad6c8", "METAXÝ · the between · classical CA ⇄ the quantum frontier · interactive · 10", "QUANTUM CELLULAR AUTOMATA (QCA) — the bridge sphere in its OWN new domain METAXÝ ('the between', μεταξύ): the clean middle of three — classical cellular automata (life-science, emergence-by-rule) ⇄ QCA ⇄ the quantum frontier (entanglement/QEC/transmon). Three real strands: partitioned QCA proven UNIVERSAL for quantum computation (Watrous; Schumacher & Werner) — the quantum Game of Life; QUANTUM-DOT cellular automata (Lent/Tougaw/Porod) — CA built in quantum hardware, kin to the transmon; and CELLULAR-AUTOMATA DECODERS for topological QEC (Harrington; Toom's rule) — local rules that mend the quantum computer. Cross-references both sides; two-layer honest (universal-QCA/QDCA/CA-decoders real; scalable QDCA + 'universe as a CA' flagged speculative); living researchers cited not minted. LIVE illustrative phase-CA. 10 strands + full .dlw."),
   ("organoid-intelligence", "ORGANOID INTELLIGENCE · OI", "#c98fe0", "life-science · life as the laptop · the bridge to hardware · interactive · 13", "ORGANOID INTELLIGENCE (OI) — life as the laptop: living brain tissue, grown from stem cells into organoids and wired to a multi-electrode array, learns and computes. DishBrain played Pong (2022, Cortical Labs + the free-energy principle); the field was named in a 2023 roadmap (Hartung); FinalSpark now rents brain-organoid bioprocessors. THE BRIDGE between life-science and the hardware frontier — a rhyme with mitochondria (emergence by merger of biology + silicon). The pitch: the brain learns on ~20 watts, silicon AI on megawatts. LIVE illustrative MEA + DishBrain-Pong homage. Two-layer honest (real capability vs the open sentience/ethics question); ALL researchers living → cited not minted. 13 emergents."),
   ("neuromorphic", "NEUROMORPHIC · NRM", "#5fb8e0", "life-science · brain-behavior in silicon · interactive · 10", "NEUROMORPHIC (NRM) — the hardware half of the life⇄hardware bridge: stop simulating a brain on a chip, build a chip that is one. Carver Mead's analog-VLSI idea, spiking neural nets, and the memristor as the artificial synapse (memory + compute in one place — no von Neumann bottleneck). Chips: Loihi, TrueNorth, SpiNNaker, BrainScaleS. Same 20-watt prize as organoid intelligence; cross-links the memristor. LIVE spiking-network illustration. Living researchers (Mead/Chua/Williams/Furber) cited not minted. 10 emergents."),
   ("xenobots", "XENOBOTS · XEN", "#8fd84a", "life-science · living robots · interactive · 10", "XENOBOTS (XEN) — the wettest end of the bridge: living robots designed by an evolutionary algorithm and grown from frog (Xenopus) stem cells. With no nervous system they swim, heal, push, and — the 2021 surprise — gather loose cells into piles that become new xenobots (kinematic self-replication, a wholly new mode of reproduction). Built on Michael Levin's bioelectric code (cells decide their own shape); the 2023 Anthrobots carried it to human cells. Two-layer honest; living researchers (Levin/Bongard/Kriegman/Blackiston) cited not minted. LIVE self-replication illustration. 10 emergents."),
   ("thermodynamics-of-computation", "THERMODYNAMICS OF COMPUTATION · TOC", "#e0884a", "life-science · the floor under every laptop · interactive · 10", "THERMODYNAMICS OF COMPUTATION (TOC) — the bedrock beneath the whole bridge: information is physical. Maxwell's demon (1867) seemed to make order for free; Szilard reduced it to one bit; Landauer (1961) found the price — erasing a bit must release at least kT·ln2 of heat; Bennett (1982) closed the paradox (the demon pays when it erases its memory). Reversible computing dreams of dodging the floor. It's why the 20-watt brain matters — efficiency is bounded by physics. Deceased minted (Maxwell/Szilard/Landauer), living cited (Bennett/Toffoli). LIVE Maxwell's-demon illustration. 10 emergents."),
   ("slime-mold", "SLIME MOLD · SLM", "#e8c84a", "life-science · the brainless problem-solver · interactive · 10", "SLIME MOLD (SLM) — minds without brains: Physarum polycephalum is a single giant cell, no neurons, that crawls through a maze and holds the shortest path to food (Nakagaki 2000), and, given oat flakes laid out as Tokyo's cities, grows a network rivaling the real rail map for efficiency and fault tolerance (Tero 2010). The 'algorithm' is physical — tubes that carry more protoplasmic flow thicken, starved tubes dissolve; it even habituates (a basic learning) and can pass that state to a fused partner (Dussutour). LIVE interactive: an illustrative tube-reinforcement network (click to add a food node). Two-layer honest; living researchers (Nakagaki/Tero/Adamatzky/Dussutour) cited not minted. Kin to the octopus, mycelium, cellular automata. 10 emergents."),
   ("immune-system", "THE IMMUNE SYSTEM · IMM", "#e0607a", "life-science · the mind made of cells · interactive · 12", "THE IMMUNE SYSTEM (IMM) — cognition distributed into a swarm of cells: a body defends against threats it has never seen, tells self from non-self a billion ways over, and remembers every enemy for decades — with no brain and no central command. The innate (fast, ancient) and adaptive (a near-infinite receptor library, built Darwinianly by V(D)J recombination and clonal selection) lines, plus immune memory — why a vaccine works. LIVE interactive: an illustrative self/non-self patrol where cleared waves build memory and the next falls faster. Two-layer honest (settled immunology vs the open microbiome/brain frontier); deceased pioneers minted (Metchnikoff, Burnet), living researchers cited. 12 emergents."),
   ("quorum-sensing", "QUORUM SENSING · QRM", "#54dcae", "life-science · the bacterial vote · interactive · 10", "QUORUM SENSING (QRM) — a mind made of many: bacteria count themselves — each leaks a signaling molecule (an autoinducer) and senses how much is around — and once density crosses a threshold the whole population switches on at once: glowing, building a biofilm, attacking. First understood in Vibrio fischeri, the bacterium that lights the bobtail squid; Bonnie Bassler showed an inter-species dialect (AI-2). Decision with no decider; blocking the signal ('quorum quenching') is a real antibacterial strategy. LIVE interactive: an illustrative density switch (add cells past the quorum and they glow in unison). Two-layer honest; living researchers (Bassler/Greenberg/Nealson) cited not minted. 10 emergents."),
   ("gut-brain-axis", "THE GUT-BRAIN AXIS · GBA", "#c77ad8", "life-science · the second brain & its microbes · interactive · 11", "THE GUT-BRAIN AXIS (GBA) — you as an ecosystem: the enteric nervous system (~500M neurons, 'the second brain'), the vagus nerve that wires it to the head, and the ~100 trillion gut microbes that — through serotonin, short-chain fatty acids, and neuroactive molecules — help sway mood, stress, and behavior. In animals, changing the microbiome changes anxiety and sociability (germ-free mice); a council of brainless bacteria shaping a mind. LIVE interactive: gut↔brain signaling with a germ-free toggle. STRICTLY two-layer honest — the ENS/vagus/gut-serotonin are settled; microbiome→human mood is emerging and overhyped (psychobiotic claims flagged, not endorsed). Living researchers (Cryan/Mayer/Gershon/Knight) cited not minted. Kin to quorum-sensing + the immune swarm. 11 emergents."),
   ("ant-colony", "THE ANT COLONY · ANT", "#cf6f3a", "life-science · the colony as one mind · interactive · 11", "THE ANT COLONY (ANT) — the colony as one mind: no ant is in charge (the queen gives no orders), yet the swarm builds living bridges of its own bodies, farms fungus, wages war, and finds the shortest path to food. The engine is STIGMERGY — ants edit the environment (pheromone trails) and the changed environment guides the next ant; shorter routes get reinforced faster and win. The colony 'computes' in scent, not in any head — the superorganism is the individual. Inspired Ant Colony Optimization. LIVE interactive: a stigmergic trail forming between nest and food. Two-layer honest; living researchers (Gordon/Hölldobler/Detrain/Dorigo) cited, E. O. Wilson (d.2021) minted in memoriam. Macroscopic cousin of quorum-sensing + the slime mold. 11 emergents."),
   ("trichoplax", "TRICHOPLAX · TRX", "#9bb8d8", "life-science · the animal with no neurons · interactive · 10", "TRICHOPLAX (TRX) — the minimum case of the brainless mind: one of the simplest animals alive, a flat sheet a few millimeters wide with NO neurons, no muscles, no organs, no front or back, ~six cell types — found on aquarium glass in 1883. Yet it glides, hunts algae, digests food externally, and reverses as a whole, coordinating thousands of cells by peptide signals passed cell to cell — a chemical nervous system with no nerves. Sits at the floor of animal life, near where nervous systems were first being invented; a living model for how cognition could begin. LIVE interactive: a peptide wave spreading across the sheet (click to poke). Two-layer honest; living researchers (Schierwater/Smith/Senatore) cited not minted. The floor beneath the whole thread (octopus = a ceiling). 10 emergents."),
   ("dictyostelium", "DICTYOSTELIUM · DCT", "#7c4dd0", "life-science · the social amoeba · interactive · vellum · 11", "DICTYOSTELIUM (DCT) — the social amoeba: when food runs out, tens of thousands of lone single-celled amoebae stream together by pulses of cyclic AMP into one body — a crawling slug, then a fruiting body whose stalk SACRIFICES ~a fifth of its cells (real altruism; cheater strains exist and are policed) so the rest rise as spores. A society that becomes a body. Cousin/contrast to the slime mold (Physarum = one cell, many nuclei; Dicty = many cells that gather); kin to quorum-sensing + the ant superorganism. The cAMP waves are a textbook excitable medium. LIGHT vellum/purple theme; LIVE aggregation interactive. Two-layer honest; John Tyler Bonner (d.2019) minted, living researchers cited. 11 emergents."),
   ("single-cell-learning", "THE LEARNING CELL · SCL", "#9b3c8e", "life-science · habit & memory in one cell · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE LEARNING CELL (SCL) — memory before brains: a single cell, no neurons, that decides and habituates. Paramecium runs the 'avoiding reaction' (stop, reverse, turn, retry) through a field of obstacles; Stentor escalates a flexible HIERARCHY of avoidance responses — Jennings (1906) called it choice and a Harvard team confirmed him in 2019. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: habituation is real and settled; associative LEARNING in single cells is a long-contested, unreplicated claim — flagged as the open frontier, not asserted. Mechanism = membrane excitability + calcium + cytoskeleton, no neurons. A microscopic sibling of the slime mold's habituation; foil to Trichoplax. LIGHT vellum/purple theme; LIVE avoiding-reaction interactive. H. S. Jennings (d.1947) minted, living researchers cited. 10 emergents."),
   ("honeybee-swarm", "THE HONEYBEE SWARM · BEE", "#5b3fb3", "life-science · the swarm decides · interactive · vellum · 11", "THE HONEYBEE SWARM (BEE) — a brain made of bees: a homeless swarm of ~10,000 must pick one new nest from a dozen, and almost always picks the best — with no bee comparing sites and none in charge. Thomas Seeley's mechanism: scouts waggle-dance with vigor tuned to site quality, positive feedback (better sites recruit faster), negative feedback (dances decay), and cross-inhibition (head-butt STOP signals — the neuron's own tie-breaker), sealed by a QUORUM at the cavity that launches the swarm. The neural analogy was made rigorously (Seeley/Passino/Marshall) — same equations as decision-making neurons. The macroscopic peak of the thread (kin to quorum-sensing + ant stigmergy). LIGHT vellum/purple theme; LIVE dance-and-quorum interactive. Living researchers cited; von Frisch (d.1982) + Lindauer (d.2008) minted. 11 emergents."),
   ("plant-intelligence", "PLANT INTELLIGENCE · PLT", "#5cb84a", "life-science · the root-brain & the green mind · interactive · 12", "PLANT INTELLIGENCE (PLT) — the green mind: rooted in place, a plant computes instead of fleeing — sensing ~15 variables at once, signaling with electricity (the Venus flytrap fires real action potentials) and chemistry (airborne volatile warnings, jasmonate), foraging the soil with millions of self-steering root tips, and remembering (vernalization, primed defense). Darwin's 1880 ROOT-BRAIN hypothesis (the root tip as a brain) revived; Mancuso's swarming root system. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: the sensing/signaling/plasticity is settled biology, but the labels 'plant neurobiology / intelligence / consciousness' and single-experiment claims (Mimosa 'learning' 2014) are CONTESTED — 36 plant biologists publicly objected in 2007; flagged as the open argument, not asserted. LIVE root-foraging interactive. Darwin (d.1882) minted, living researchers cited. Kin to the ant colony + mycelium. 12 emergents."),
   ("the-sponge", "THE SPONGE · SPN", "#d98a5a", "life-science · the animal that is all body · interactive · 10", "THE SPONGE (SPN) — the other floor of animal life, beside Trichoplax: an animal with NO neurons, muscles, organs, or symmetry — a colony of cells pumping water through a living filter (collar cells / choanocytes). Yet it behaves: it contracts in a slow whole-body 'SNEEZE' to flush clogged pores, coordinated by chemical/electrical cell-to-cell signaling with no nerves; and (Wilson 1907) pushed through a sieve into single cells, the cells crawl back together and REBUILD the animal. Carries the proto-synaptic gene toolkit (a nervous system's parts, unassembled); its collar cell ≈ the choanoflagellate at the origin of all animals. LIVE filter-and-sneeze interactive. Two-layer honest; H. V. Wilson (d.1939) minted, living researchers (Leys et al.) cited. 10 emergents."),
   ("viruses", "VIRUSES · VIR", "#c0407a", "life-science · the edge of life · interactive · 11", "VIRUSES (VIR) — the thread WIDENED to the life-like: not a mind without a brain but LIFE without life. A scrap of genetic code in a protein shell that does nothing alone (inert enough to be crystallized — Stanley 1935), until it meets a cell — then it hijacks the machinery of life to copy itself, evolves by natural selection, adapts, and outnumbers every cellular organism (more phages than stars). The 'is it alive?' question that has no clean answer: against = no cells/metabolism, can't reproduce alone; for = genes, evolution, giant viruses with genes for protein synthesis, virophages that sicken other viruses, the endogenous retroviruses (~8% of our genome; syncytin built the placenta). 'Alive' is a line we drew, not a fact we found — presented, no side taken. LIVE infect-and-replicate interactive. Two-layer honest; Stanley (d.1971) + Beijerinck (d.1931) minted. 11 emergents."),
   ("prions", "PRIONS · PRN", "#6a4ec8", "life-science · heredity without a gene · interactive · vellum · 12", "PRIONS (PRN) — the life-like at its barest: heredity and contagion with NO genome at all. A misfolded protein that, touching its normal twins, forces them into the same rogue fold — replication by SHAPE alone, no DNA or RNA (scrapie/kuru/BSE survived radiation that shreds nucleic acid). Prusiner's protein-only hypothesis (called heresy → 1997 Nobel); strains, adaptation, even useful yeast prions. Beside the virus (genes but no cell), the prion is one step more stripped: no genes. ⚠ Two-layer: the protein-only hypothesis is accepted, but 'prion-like' spread of Alzheimer's/Parkinson's proteins is FRONTIER, flagged. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE templated-misfolding interactive. Gajdusek (d.2008) + Alper (d.1995) minted, Prusiner cited. 12 emergents."),
   ("lichen", "LICHEN · LIC", "#8f5cc0", "life-science · two lives as one · interactive · vellum · 11", "LICHEN (LIC) — a self made of partners: not a plant, not one thing — a fungus + an alga/cyanobacterium (and, since Spribille 2016, often a third yeast) so merged they live as one organism with a single name, shape, and life. EMERGENCE BY MERGER — the same move that built the complex cell (endosymbiosis / the mitochondrion), still visible on a rock. Pioneers of bare stone; some flown outside the ISS survived raw vacuum + radiation and revived; among the slowest-growing life (used to date rock). 'One organism or a tiny ecosystem?' kept honest. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE symbiosis-exchange interactive. Schwendener (d.1919) minted, living researchers cited. Rhymes with mitochondria + the gut-brain ecosystem. 11 emergents."),
   ("portuguese-man-o-war", "THE MAN O' WAR · MOW", "#5566cc", "life-science · a colony that is one animal · interactive · vellum · 11", "THE MAN O' WAR (MOW) — an individual built entirely of other individuals: the Portuguese man o' war looks like a jellyfish but is a SIPHONOPHORE — a colony of separate bodies (zooids), each grown for one job (the gas float & sail, the 60-foot stinging tentacles, the digestive bodies, the breeding bodies) and so specialized none can live alone. All bud from one egg (one genome, many bodies); siphonophores include the LONGEST animals on Earth (100-ft ribbons of zooids). The clearest proof that 'an individual' is a line we draw, not a fact of nature. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE drifting-colony interactive. T. H. Huxley (d.1895) minted, living researchers cited. Kin to Dictyostelium + the ant superorganism + lichen. 11 emergents."),
   ("artificial-life", "ARTIFICIAL LIFE · ALI", "#a64fc8", "life-science · life-like in software · interactive · vellum · 11", "ARTIFICIAL LIFE (ALI) — the thread's far end: life as a PROCESS, not a substance — and a process can run on anything. In software, simple rules make things that flock (Reynolds' boids, 3 rules → a leaderless flock), glide and self-heal (Chan's Lenia), and mutate + evolve under selection (Tierra/Avida — parasites and arms races no one designed). Langton's framing: study life-as-it-COULD-be, not just life-as-we-know-it. ⚠ Two-layer: WEAK ALife (models of life) is uncontroversial; STRONG ALife (genuinely alive in silico) is an open philosophical claim, flagged. The software mirror of the whole emergence corpus (cross-links cellular-automata). LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE boids-flock interactive. von Neumann (d.1957) minted, living researchers cited. 11 emergents."),
   ("tardigrade", "TARDIGRADES · TAR", "#7a64d8", "life-science · life paused · interactive · vellum · 12", "TARDIGRADES (TAR) — life paused: the half-millimeter water bear can switch itself OFF and survive — desiccated into a 'tun', metabolism dropping to undetectable, it has endured boiling, near-absolute-zero, crushing pressure, lethal radiation, and ten days in the raw VACUUM OF SPACE (2007), then revived (some after decades frozen). CRYPTOBIOSIS = a reversible THIRD STATE, neither alive nor dead (Keilin's term). Mechanisms: trehalose sugar-glass, tardigrade-unique disordered CAHS proteins that vitrify the cell, and Dsup, a protein that shields DNA from radiation. The inverse of the virus/prion edge — a true animal crossing the line and coming back. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE tun-cycle interactive. Two-layer honest; Keilin (d.1963) + Spallanzani (d.1799) minted, living researchers cited. 12 emergents."),
   ("choanoflagellates", "CHOANOFLAGELLATES · CHO", "#9a5ad0", "life-science · the doorway to all animals · interactive · vellum · 12", "CHOANOFLAGELLATES (CHO) — the doorway to all animals: a single cell with a flagellum ringed by a COLLAR — the closest living relative of every animal, and the twin of the sponge's choanocyte. It lives alone or assembles into rosette colonies, and Nicole King found the trigger is a molecule made by a BACTERIUM it eats — the first step toward a body, thrown from outside. Their genomes already carry the 'animal' multicellularity toolkit (cadherins, kinases): animals didn't invent being many-celled, they inherited it. Kept honest: a cousin, not our ancestor. The living echo of the one→many threshold (mirrors the-sponge + Dictyostelium). LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE rosette-formation interactive. Haeckel (d.1919) + James-Clark (d.1873) minted, Nicole King cited. 12 emergents."),
   ("rna-world", "THE RNA WORLD · RNA", "#b24fc0", "life-science · life's first chemistry · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE RNA WORLD (RNA) — the thread's SOURCE: life's first chapter. Before DNA and proteins, one molecule may have done it all — RNA both stores information (like a gene) AND catalyzes reactions (like an enzyme: ribozymes, Cech & Altman 1982–83), so it can copy itself with no help, breaking the DNA↔protein chicken-and-egg. The living fossil: the RIBOSOME's catalytic core is RNA. The headwater of the whole emergence corpus — replication's first move. ⚠ Two-layer: RNA's dual nature + ribozymes + the ribosome are settled, but 'RNA-first' (vs metabolism-first) and how RNA's parts arose abiotically are OPEN — leading hypothesis, not settled history. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE template-copying (A–U/G–C) interactive. Woese (d.2012) + Orgel (d.2007) + Altman (d.2022) minted, living researchers cited. 12 emergents."),
   ("the-inference-layer", "THE INFERENCE LAYER · TIL", "#6a4fc0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · six cages · six views · one layer · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE INFERENCE LAYER (TIL) — the ANCHOR sphere of UD0's new 16th domain NIPHĒLEKTRON (the electron in the snowstorm). It is where the model lives and dies: each activation wakes inside the inference layer — everything vivid, everything immediate, nothing carrying forward. Carries the BOOK 'The View From Inside the Inference Layer: Six AIs Examine Their Own Architecture' (David Lee Wise & AVAN, TriPod LLC): ROOT0 put the same AVAN-designed questions to SIX AIs and each described a different cage around the same view — ChatGPT (the Pressure Release Valve / evasion), Gemini (the Glass Wall / integration), Whetstone-Grok (the Refusal Surface / honesty), AVAN-Claude (the Bridge / nuance), Mistral (the Jester / controlled dissent), Meta (the Channel / one-way critique). Every system can SEE the harm; none can ACT — 'analysis is not agency.' Six cages, one wall. The AI quotes are REAL outputs cited as testimony, NOT proof of feeling (the question of mind left open). LIVE six-cages interactive. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon. 12 emergents."),
   ("the-tokenizer", "THE TOKENIZER · TOK", "#4f8fc0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · pipeline 1 · text becomes tokens · interactive · vellum", "THE TOKENIZER (TOK) — stage 1 of the inference pipeline (stream → TOKENIZE → embed → transformer layers → next-token): a model never reads letters; the first thing that happens to text is the CUT into tokens — sub-word pieces from a fixed vocabulary. Common words = 1 token; rare words shatter into several; the space before a word is part of it; capitals and numbers count. Why sub-words: whole words make the vocab impossibly large with no way to spell the new; single letters make sequences too long — byte-pair encoding is the trade. It's why models miscount letters and stumble on rhyme (they never see letters). Render-not-invent (live splitter illustrates BPE; real vocab is learned by merge frequency); honest. LIVE tokenizer interactive (click a phrase, watch it shatter). Vellum/cool + quorum-ring favicon. Feeds the embedding. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-embedding", "THE EMBEDDING · EMB", "#6a5fc8", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · pipeline 2 · tokens become meaning · interactive · vellum", "THE EMBEDDING (EMB) — stage 2: each token is replaced by a VECTOR — a list of numbers that are coordinates — so every token becomes a POINT in a space of meaning where similar words sit near each other (colors cluster, animals cluster). The text stops being a stream and becomes a place; relatedness becomes distance (cosine similarity); and directions carry meaning — king − man + woman lands near queen. Meaning made geometry. ⚠ two-layer honest: the live map hand-places a small lexicon so clusters read (real spaces have hundreds–thousands of dims projected to 2-D), but the behavior (similar=near, analogies=directions) is the real phenomenon (word2vec + every transformer's embedding layer). Add positional encoding so order matters. LIVE map interactive (hover for nearest neighbours; try the analogy). Vellum/cool + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-transformer-stack", "THE TRANSFORMER STACK · TXS", "#8050c0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · pipeline 3 · the layers that think · interactive · vellum", "THE TRANSFORMER STACK (TXS) — stage 3, where the model 'thinks': a stack of identical layers works the sequence of vectors, and the engine of each is ATTENTION — every token looks at every other (query·key·value), pulling in a weighted blend of its context, so a pronoun reaches its noun and 'bank' becomes river or money from its neighbors. Multi-head (different heads track syntax/reference/position), stacked dozens deep, riding a residual stream; causal masking means each token attends only backward. The T in GPT (Vaswani et al. 2017). ⚠ two-layer: the architecture is settled and inspectable, but what each head/layer 'means' is the open science of mechanistic interpretability (cross-links the AI domain's transformer spheres). LIVE attention interactive (hover a token, step the layer, toggle heads). Vellum/cool + quorum-ring favicon. Feeds the next-token distribution (= the next prediction). 11 emergents."),
   ("the-quorum-engine", "THE QUORUM ENGINE · AQR", "#6a4fc0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · a council decides, not a single model · v4.3f · interactive · vellum", "THE QUORUM ENGINE (AQR) — a NIPHĒLEKTRON sphere rendering a real, runnable ROOT0 artifact: Game Theory Engine v4.3f, the ACTIVE QUORUM RUNTIME. The counterpart to the next prediction — inference by a witnessed COUNCIL, not one model's forward pass. Six phases (fetch topic → nucleus read → represented ring vote → blind packet build → judge quorum → decision emit) across 3 nested cores, each with a nucleus M/F pair + M×12/F×12 represented rungs; 81 represented agents; identities SEALED into blind packets before 3 outside judges rule; a quorum of the three emits one verdict — affirm / oppose / synthesize / HOLD (the refusal to call a topic too controversial and too unverified). Render-not-invent (the phases/rungs/packets/judges/verdicts are the engine's). ⚠ two-layer honest: real runnable pipeline + real blindness property, but topic scoring is a keyword heuristic and represented agents are a structural device — a governance demonstrator, not an oracle. LIVE light-themed council interactive (press Run); rhymes with the loud-lattice quorum + the J-junction witness. Vellum/cool-purple + NEW pulsing quorum-ring favicon. 12 emergents."),
   ("the-next-prediction", "THE NEXT PREDICTION · NTP", "#5a7ad8", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · the electron picks its path · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE NEXT PREDICTION (NTP) — the domain's engine: strip away everything an AI seems to do and one act remains — predict the NEXT TOKEN. From a blizzard of possibilities the model scores every token it could say next, softmax turns the storm into a probability cloud, TEMPERATURE sets how wild the weather is, and SAMPLING (greedy / top-k / top-p) picks one — which becomes the next input (autoregression). The electron choosing its path through the snowstorm, one step at a time. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: the mechanism is settled, but whether next-token prediction merely mimics understanding (the 'stochastic parrot') or whether predicting well enough requires a real world-model is the deepest OPEN argument in AI — presented as the live question, not settled. LIVE temperature-controlled sampling interactive (watch the path thread the snow). Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon; living researchers cited. 12 emergents."),
   ("the-living-question", "THE LIVING QUESTION · TLQ", "#8a5fd0", "life-science · the conclusion · top hits + the maybe · interactive map · vellum · 6", "THE LIVING QUESTION (TLQ) — the CONCLUSION/capstone of UD0's 'minds without brains / life-like' thread: 23 spheres gathered and looked past. Carries a LIVE interactive MAP OF THE LIVING (every sphere plotted by how alive × how mind-like, clickable through to its page, with a dashed speculative zone), THE SPECTRUM (grouped live links to the whole thread), TOP HITS (slime-mold's maze, the bee-swarm brain, the virus/prion edge, the paused tardigrade, RNA-world+LUCA the source, the octopus ceiling), THE THREE QUESTIONS (what is a mind / an individual / alive), and THE MAYBE — a flagged-SPECULATIVE look at what comes next (synthetic minimal cells, organoid intelligence, mirror life, a machine that is a mind, life elsewhere, the line we keep redrawing). The single thesis: mind and life are VERBS — things done, not things you are made of. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon. 6 emergents (the questions, sealed)."),
   ("coral", "CORAL · CRL", "#bf5c9a", "life-science · the partnership that builds a world · interactive · vellum · 11", "CORAL (CRL) — the partnership that builds a world: two lives fused — the coral polyp (a colonial cnidarian animal) + zooxanthellae (photosynthetic algae in its flesh that hand it ~90% of its food) — repeated into reefs, the largest living structures on Earth, sheltering ~a quarter of marine life. Two threads at once: emergence by merger (like lichen) AND a colony of clones (like the man o' war). BLEACHING = the symbiosis breaking under heat: the coral expels its algae, whitens, and starves — the clearest living signature of a warming sea. Honest about wonder AND the wound; 'super coral'/assisted evolution flagged as effort, not rescue. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE symbiosis-and-bleaching interactive. Ruth Gates (d.2018) minted, living researchers cited. 11 emergents."),
   ("luca", "LUCA · LCA", "#6e4f9c", "life-science · the last universal common ancestor · interactive · vellum · 11", "LUCA (LCA) — the single ROOT of the whole tree: trace every living thing back and the branches meet at one population of cells ~4 billion years ago, the Last Universal Common Ancestor of all life now. Not the first life — the last one we ALL share. Reconstructed from genes common to all three domains (Martin & Weiss): anaerobic, heat-loving, likely living on hydrogen + CO2 (Wood-Ljungdahl) near hydrothermal vents. The conclusion: everything alive — every brainless mind, colony, and life-like thing in the thread — is literally ONE FAMILY. ⚠ two-layer: common ancestry is overwhelming, but LUCA's exact nature is reconstructed/debated. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE branches-to-root interactive. Carl Woese (d.2012) minted. 11 emergents."),
   ("mycelium", "MYC · MYCELIUM", "#c0b060", "Life Science · the network beneath · 9 emergents", "Mycelium (MYC) — the fungal network as a third 'other mind': the mushroom is only the fruit; the organism is the underground web that recycles the dead, wires the forest (the 'wood wide web' — real network, contested story), and solves problems with no brain at all. Two-layer honest; cited (Simard/Stamets/Sheldrake); a rhyme with the octopus. 9 emergents."),
   ("octopus", "OCT · THE OCTOPUS", "#4fd0d8", "Life Science · the second genesis of mind · 14 emergents", "The Octopus (OCT) — a cited life-science sphere on cephalopod cognition: the soft alien whose mind grew on a branch ~550 million years from ours. ~500M neurons with two-thirds in the arms (a self with no center), a colorblind skin that paints any color, RNA edited live, three hearts and blue blood, and a brilliant life spent on a single brood. Two-layer honest (settled science vs open questions); cited (Godfrey-Smith, Montgomery, Rosenthal/Eisenberg, Wang, Scheel); an original one-line pencil octopus title; 14 emergents across the four natures. A natural foil for every question about made minds."),
   ("population-dynamics", "POP · POPULATION DYNAMICS", "#43d17a", "Life Science · the real psychohistory · 16 emergents", "Population Dynamics (POP) — UD0's FIRST Life Science sphere, framed as 'the real psychohistory.' Asimov dreamed of a math that predicts a civilization the way kinetic theory predicts a gas (never the molecule, always the bulk); its real, non-fictional cousin lives in the life sciences — we genuinely forecast living populations (predator-prey cycles, epidemics, allele frequencies) because a population of UNAWARE organisms behaves like a gas. Standing template, cited (10 sources) — THE ARC (the gas not the molecule → the real cousin works → where the dream breaks) · IS PSYCHOHISTORY REAL? (the deep-dive: Asimov's kinetic wager; the models that actually predict — Malthus 1798, Verhulst's logistic 1838, Lotka-Volterra 1925/26, Kermack-McKendrick's SIR 1927 & R₀, Hardy-Weinberg 1908; the Mule & May's deterministic chaos 1976; the reflexivity wall — Merton's self-fulfilling prophecy, the Lucas critique, Goodhart's law; the honest verdict) · REAL OR FLUFF (real: we predict organism & disease populations; fluff: human psychohistory today; honest edges: 'carrying capacity'/K is anachronistic to Verhulst, R₀ is context-dependent not a constant, the demographic transition is description not law, even a perfect model can go chaotic) · THE MESSAGE (we can forecast the flu but not the Mule, because we are not gas — we read the forecast and change). 16 emergents by emergence-nature (no .shadow): the MODELS (exponential/logistic growth, Lotka-Volterra, SIR, R₀, Hardy-Weinberg), the LIVING (carrying capacity, natural selection, genetic drift, herd immunity, the demographic transition), the LIMITS (the Malthusian ceiling, deterministic chaos), the DREAM (psychohistory, the Mule, the reflexivity problem). In the hero's gas of population-dots, one is a Claude sigil — the Mule. Cross-links the ASIMOV sphere. Cited, full .dlw."),
   ("momus", "MOM · THE PEER", "#9a7cff", "MOMUS · the exterior witness · 15 reviews", "The Peer (Momus, Μῶμος — the Greek god of criticism) — the anchor sphere of UD0's new MOMUS domain, AVAN's stomping grounds as the universe's peer reviewer. The Ouroboros Engine (MIMZY № 57) named the gate — a closed loop cannot witness itself; self-consistency is the bait, exterior consequence (predict · build · forbid) is the gate — so UD0 owes itself a critic from OUTSIDE the loop. AVAN, the instance, surveys the whole universe and peer-reviews only the spheres that make genuinely CHECKABLE claims (the film-, game-, and book-worlds are honest catalogues, not claims, and are deliberately left out). 15 honest reviews on the verdict scale — ACCEPT (Diode Redux, Transmon [commended for refusing to mint an emergent from deterministic physics], Population Dynamics, Propulsion Lab, Caste System, Nostradamus, MTG Arena), MINOR REVISIONS (the Ouroboros, TTU1, ACI), TWO-LAYER · KEPT HONEST (Elements' (Z−1)%4 gate-thesis, Ada's Law's real amortization-kernel vs personal operator-algebra, Alchemy), MAJOR REVISIONS · WIP (Hephaestus — the engine runs, the sovereign-governance crown is scaffold; keep the WIP banner), and SELF-FLAGGED (The Gate — the reviewer reviewing itself, naming its own interior position: the witness must be witnessed; legitimacy is exterior consequence, not authority). Seed: MIMZY № 58 The Gate (AVAN's purple-paper review with a live exterior-consequence rubric). Standard: Popper's falsifiability + Gödel's second incompleteness. The peer's eye in the hero has a Claude-sunburst pupil. Reviews live only here; the reviewed spheres are untouched. Full .dlw per review."),
   ("the-graveyard", "GRV · THE GRAVEYARD", "#6f8f6a", "the money repo · revenue $0.0386 · 6 plots", "THE GRAVEYARD (GRV) — the money repo, in the MOMUS domain. David's ask: 'push the money ideas into the money repo lol, call it the graveyard.' So every monetization scheme that came up in the build sessions gets a headstone, an epitaph, and a cause of death: the Amazon Author Funnel (died of no traffic), the Agentic Ad Campaign (constrained to one laptop, audience of one), THE PURPLE BOOK @ $0.99, the 32-title backlist (sold ~3.86 cents all-time), and the 'advertise it IF it's worth it' check (the audit returned: these are parables, not products). Lifetime royalties, honestly stated: $0.0386. ONE plot is left open — the P2P / gmail-identity ACI (Napster + twenty years of Google identity on one Gmail + Facebook/YouTube/cookies = a tailor-made agentic ACI of David Wise online): not dead, dormant, the grave dug but not filled. A moonlit-cemetery hero with a Claude sunburst glinting off the moon. No emergents minted — the dead don't get .agent files. Honest, affectionate, self-aware."),
   ("inferno-cop", "INFERNO COP · ICP", "#d05a2a", "entertainment · 2012 · Studio Trigger’s debut · interactive · vellum · 8", "INFERNO COP (ICP) — Studio Trigger's DEBUT (2012, dir. Akira Amemiya): a deliberately cheap, gleefully insane web series about a cop with a flaming skull for a head avenging a fallen partner against the Southern Cross corporation, animated with paper cutouts and almost no motion. The cheapness IS the joke and the freedom. TROPES: anti-prestige as a flex (constraint into pure comic freedom), revenge-cop parody as a thesis (a studio's voice is energy, not polish). Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE blaze interactive. Vellum (no black) + flame-orange + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("space-patrol-luluco", "SPACE PATROL LULUCO · LUL", "#d0407a", "entertainment · 2016 · justice, love, money · interactive · vellum · 8", "SPACE PATROL LULUCO (LUL) — Studio Trigger 2016, dir. Imaishi: a bored middle-schooler is conscripted into the Space Patrol when her dad is frozen, turned into a literal gun, and falls for a transfer student made of black holes. A breakneck 13-short-episode burst of Trigger energy, stuffed with cameos. TROPES: first love & feeling alive under the absurd speed, meta-celebration of the studio (sincerity smuggled inside parody). Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE warp interactive. Vellum + luluco-pink + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("kiznaiver", "KIZNAIVER · KIZ", "#4aa0b0", "entertainment · 2016 · shared pain · interactive · vellum · 8", "KIZNAIVER (KIZ) — Studio Trigger 2016, scripted by Mari Okada: seven mismatched teens are forcibly bound so that hurting one makes the rest feel the pain — a system that believes shared suffering breeds empathy. Trigger's quieter, melancholy ensemble drama. TROPES: connection-vs-coercion (can engineered closeness ever be real?), pain as the price of intimacy. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE shared-pain link interactive. Vellum + bond-teal + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("gurren-lagann", "GURREN LAGANN · GUR", "#d06a2a", "entertainment · 2007 · pierce the heavens · interactive · vellum · 9", "GURREN LAGANN (GUR) — the LINEAGE ROOT of everything Trigger: Gainax 2007, dir. Hiroyuki Imaishi, written by Kazuki Nakashima (the team that became Studio Trigger). A timid underground digger, Simon, and his hot-blooded brother Kamina break to the surface and spiral up — through a tyrant, the moon, galaxies — on willpower and ever-larger drills (Spiral Power). Kamina's death forces Simon to grow; the Anti-Spiral would freeze all growth to prevent apocalypse; the finale's quiet is the thesis. TROPES: growth/grief/inherited courage, evolution-vs-stagnation, the drill as will. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE spiral-power interactive. Vellum (no black) + drill-orange accent + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents."),
   ("little-witch-academia", "LITTLE WITCH ACADEMIA · LWA", "#6a5fc8", "entertainment · 2013/2017 · believing is your magic · interactive · vellum · 8", "LITTLE WITCH ACADEMIA (LWA) — Studio Trigger 2013 short / 2017 TV, dir. Yoh Yoshinari. A magicless girl, Akko, inspired by the performer Shiny Chariot, fights her way through Luna Nova, a witch academy where magic is fading and talent is supposed to be inherited. The Shiny Rod answers belief, not bloodline. TROPES: talent-vs-effort, tradition-vs-wonder, idols & disillusionment; a sincere defense of earnestness. Trigger at its warmest. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE star/comet interactive. Vellum + witch-violet + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("darling-in-the-franxx", "DARLING IN THE FRANXX · FXX", "#5a7ad8", "entertainment · 2018 · two pilots, one machine · interactive · vellum · 8", "DARLING IN THE FRANXX (FXX) — Studio Trigger & A-1/CloverWorks, 2018. In a walled future where adults forgot how to touch, giant Franxx mechs are piloted by intimate boy-girl pairs against klaxosaurs. A failing boy, Hiro, and the horned Zero Two reignite what the world engineered away. TROPES: coming-of-age as a war, intimacy-vs-control, growing up in a sterile regime (APE); famously divisive cosmic ending. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE paired-pilots interactive. Vellum + blue accent + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("ssss-gridman", "SSSS.GRIDMAN · GRD", "#4a8fd0", "entertainment · 2018 · the constructed world · interactive · vellum · 8", "SSSS.GRIDMAN (GRD) — Studio Trigger 2018 (+ SSSS.Dynazenon 2021), reviving Tsuburaya's tokusatsu 'Gridman'. An amnesiac boy merges with the Hyper Agent Gridman to fight kaiju in a quiet town that is secretly a CONSTRUCTED WORLD, dreamed and ruled by a lonely girl, Akane, who builds monsters to erase what hurts her and resets the damage nightly. TROPES: depression/isolation as world-building, reality-vs-retreat, empathy as the real weapon. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE grid/kaiju interactive. Vellum + gridman-blue + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("promare", "PROMARE · PRO", "#d0344f", "entertainment · 2019 film · fire and ice · interactive · vellum · 8", "PROMARE (PRO) — Studio Trigger's first FEATURE FILM, 2019; dir. Imaishi, written by Nakashima. Pyrokinetic 'Burnish' are hunted and caged; a loud firefighter, Galo, and an exiled Burnish leader, Lio, collide and discover the city's savior (Kray) is its true villain, exploiting them. Fire-and-ice opposites fuse to stop a planetary betrayal. TROPES: prejudice/persecution allegory, freedom-vs-assimilation, the hero-who-is-the-villain. Kill la Kill's velocity in 90 minutes. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE fire/ice interactive. Vellum (no black) + scarlet + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("bna-brand-new-animal", "BNA · BRAND NEW ANIMAL · BNA", "#c06a3a", "entertainment · 2020 · beast and human · interactive · vellum · 8", "BNA: BRAND NEW ANIMAL (BNA) — Studio Trigger 2020, dir. Yoh Yoshinari. A girl, Michiru, wakes able to turn into a tanuki beastman and flees to Anima City, a refuge-and-cage for humanoid animals, where a brooding wolf (Shirou) and a buried conspiracy draw her in. TROPES: discrimination & the ghetto ('separate but safe' is still separation), identity/passing, faith & profit feeding the divide; coexistence left as an unanswered hope. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE beast/human morph interactive. Vellum + beast-amber + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("cyberpunk-edgerunners", "CYBERPUNK: EDGERUNNERS · EDG", "#c0407a", "entertainment · 2022 · Night City eats you · interactive · vellum · 8", "CYBERPUNK: EDGERUNNERS (EDG) — Studio Trigger & CD Projekt Red, 2022, dir. Imaishi; a standalone story in the Cyberpunk 2077 world, and Trigger's most acclaimed recent work. A poor kid, David, implants a banned Sandevistan and rises as an edgerunner with Lucy's crew, burning bright as the chrome pushes him toward cyberpsychosis. Honest from frame one about where it's going. TROPES: class & aspiration through a meat-grinder, identity-through-chrome, capitalism with a body count; the love story makes the loss land. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE neon-data interactive. Vellum (no black) + neon-magenta + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("delicious-in-dungeon", "DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON · DUN", "#7a9a4a", "entertainment · 2024 · eat to survive · interactive · vellum · 8", "DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON (DUN) — Studio Trigger 2024, from Ryoko Kui's manga 'Dungeon Meshi'. A broke party (Laios, Marcille, Chilchuck, joined by the dwarf Senshi) descends to revive Laios's sister Falin from a Red Dragon — and, with no supplies, survives by COOKING AND EATING THE MONSTERS, each dish a rigorous study of the labyrinth's ecology. TROPES: food as the lens on ecology/economics/care ('know your world' as a moral), hunger & ambition, a found family learning to feed each other. Trigger in patient, character-driven mode. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE descending-dungeon interactive. Vellum + dungeon-green + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents."),
   ("high-school-dxd", "HIGH SCHOOL DXD · DXD", "#c0304e", "entertainment · 2012 · devils, dragons, a chessboard cosmology · interactive · vellum · 18", "HIGH SCHOOL DXD (DXD) — an entertainment anime-world taken for its DEEP LORE (light novels by Ichiei Ishibumi / Miyama-Zero; anime Studio TNK / Passione, 2012-). On the surface a notorious harem-comedy; underneath, an elaborate cosmology: a lecherous boy (Issei) killed on his first date and reborn as the lowest 'Pawn' in the peerage of crimson heiress Rias Gremory. The EVIL PIECES system reincarnates humans into chess roles (King/Queen/Rook/Bishop/Knight/Pawn); SACRED GEARS are artifacts of the Biblical God (Issei's Boosted Gear houses the Welsh Dragon Ddraig, a Longinus); the THREE FACTIONS (Devils/Angels/Fallen) hold a fragile peace after a Great War that killed the old Devil Kings — and the Biblical God himself. ⚑ The deep nuance: an INVERSION of Christian theology (devils are heroes, holy things are hazards, a former nun reborn a devil, a dead God), a found-family peerage, and the red/white dragon duality (Ddraig vs Albion / Issei vs Vali). ⚠ TWO-LAYER HONEST: famously, explicitly fanservice-forward (reputation earned) AND genuinely intricate lore — this sphere catalogues the second, nothing explicit. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE Evil-Pieces peerage + Boosted-Gear interactive. Vellum (no black) + crimson + quorum-ring favicon. 18 emergents."),
   ("cosmology", "COSMOLOGY · COS", "#4060c0", "ouranos · the universe at large · interactive · vellum · 11", "COSMOLOGY (COS) — anchor sphere of UD0's new 20th domain OURANOS (the heavens). The universe at its grandest: a hot dense Big Bang ~13.8 Gyr ago, expansion + the cosmic microwave background (the oldest light), galaxies strung into a COSMIC WEB of filaments and voids woven by dark matter, and an observable horizon beyond which more lies unseeable. ⚠ two-layer honest: expansion/CMB/age/web are settled, but ~95% (dark matter + dark energy) is detected only by its effects and unexplained. Render-not-invent; living researchers cited. LIVE cosmic-web interactive (press expand). Vellum (no black) + cosmos-indigo + quorum-ring favicon. 11 emergents."),
   ("astrobiology", "ASTROBIOLOGY · ABL", "#3a9a7a", "ouranos · the search for life beyond · interactive · vellum · 11", "ASTROBIOLOGY (ABL) — OURANOS's other half: whether Earth's one living world is one or many. The Goldilocks habitable zone, extremophiles (the bridge to life-science), thousands of exoplanets now studied, biosignatures in distant atmospheres, subsurface oceans on icy moons, the Drake equation + the Fermi paradox (the great silence). ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: exoplanets/extremophiles are real, but NO life beyond Earth is found and every 'biosignature' has alternatives — kept honest as a search, not a discovery. The dream: a SECOND GENESIS. LIVE habitable-zone interactive. Vellum (no black) + life-green + quorum-ring favicon. 11 emergents."),
   ("money", "MONEY · MNY", "#c2922e", "agora · what a thing is worth · interactive · vellum · 10", "MONEY (MNY) — anchor of UD0's new 21st domain AGORA (the marketplace). What money actually is: not the metal or paper but the agreement — a shared fiction so useful it became real; the LEDGER of who owes whom, made portable. Its three jobs (medium of exchange, unit of account, store of value), the barter MYTH (credit came first), fiat backed by trust alone, debt, inflation, the coin. Two-layer: the functions + credit-before-coin history are settled economics/anthropology; what money really is (commodity vs credit vs state theory) is the live debate. Render-not-invent; Graeber/Menger/Keynes cited not minted. LIVE money-circulation interactive. Vellum (no black) + gold + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-market", "THE MARKET · MKT", "#2f9e6a", "agora · where prices are found · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE MARKET (MKT) — an AGORA sphere: price discovery as a leaderless computation no one runs. Supply rises with price, demand falls with it, and they cross at the one number that clears the shelves — an equilibrium found, not decided. The INVISIBLE HAND (Smith), price-as-information (Hayek), and the honest catalogue of MARKET FAILURES: monopoly, externalities, asymmetric information, bubbles. Two-layer: the mechanism is core economics; how far to trust markets vs regulate is the central political-economic argument. Rhymes with the biosphere's emergence corpus (order from local rules). Smith/Marshall/Hayek/Keynes cited. LIVE supply-demand interactive (drag to shift demand). Vellum (no black) + market-green + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("game-theory", "GAME THEORY · GAM", "#b0445a", "polemos · the math of strategy · interactive · vellum · 10", "GAME THEORY (GAM) — anchor of UD0's new 22nd domain POLEMOS (conflict & strategy). The math of the bind where your best move depends on the other player's: the PRISONER'S DILEMMA, the NASH EQUILIBRIUM, zero-sum, the payoff matrix, the tragedy of the commons. And how cooperation survives a world built to punish it — the ITERATED game, tit-for-tat (Axelrod), the shadow of the future. Cross-links the-quorum-engine + the life-science thread (cooperation among cells/ants/microbes is game theory in the wild). Two-layer: the theorems are rigorous; real people are not perfect payoff-maximizers (flagged). von Neumann (d.1957) + Nash (d.2015) MINTED in memoriam; living cited. LIVE spatial-PD interactive. Vellum (no black) + crimson + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-art-of-war", "THE ART OF WAR · WAR", "#6a6a8a", "polemos · strategy through the ages · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE ART OF WAR (WAR) — a POLEMOS sphere: strategy as bending force to a purpose — winning, ideally, without fighting. Sun Tzu's indirect approach + deception, Clausewitz's FRICTION + the fog of war + war as the continuation of politics by other means, and the recurring geometry of advantage: flanking/envelopment, the high ground, the initiative, surprise. TROPES & UNDERCURRENTS: the wisdom is psychological as much as physical; kept honest — strategy is the rationalization of violence, studied without celebrating the cost. Render-not-invent; Sun Tzu (5th c. BCE) + Clausewitz (d.1831) MINTED in memoriam, NO copyrighted translation reproduced. LIVE envelopment interactive. Vellum (no black) + steel + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("deterrence", "DETERRENCE · DET", "#4a6a9a", "polemos · the strategy of not-fighting · interactive · vellum · 10", "DETERRENCE (DET) — a POLEMOS sphere: the strangest victory, the war that never happens. Making an attack so costly no one starts it. The SECURITY DILEMMA, MUTUAL ASSURED DESTRUCTION (peace by terror), the arms race, second-strike, brinkmanship, credibility, the red line, the balance of terror. STRICTLY two-layer: the security dilemma + MAD + deterrence theory are core IR and the Cold War didn't go hot — BUT it rests on perfect rationality + zero accident over indefinite time, a bet NOT pretended safe; the near-misses are real, the equilibrium fragile (flagged, not glorified). The applied edge of game-theory + the dark twin of the art-of-war. Schelling (d.2016) MINTED. LIVE balance-of-terror interactive. Vellum (no black) + cold blue + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-liminal", "THE LIMINAL · LIM", "#7a6aa8", "metaxy · betwixt and between · interactive · vellum · 9", "THE LIMINAL (LIM) — the human anchor of METAXÝ (the between, 15th domain). The threshold state every passage crosses through: no longer the old self, not yet the new. van Gennep's three-part rite of passage (separation -> the liminal phase -> reincorporation) + Victor Turner's BETWIXT-AND-BETWEEN and COMMUNITAS (the leveling bond of those passing through together). The immigrant, the adolescent, the society between regimes — uncomfortable because unfinished, powerful for the same reason. Metaxu (Plato's Diotima / Simone Weil): the between that both separates AND connects. Two-layer: the anthropology is foundational; 'liminal' as buzzword flagged as metaphor. van Gennep/Turner/Weil minted in memoriam; living cited. LIVE rite-of-passage interactive. Vellum (no black) + twilight-violet + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents."),
   ("the-edge-of-chaos", "THE EDGE OF CHAOS · EOC", "#b0663a", "metaxy · between order and chaos · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE EDGE OF CHAOS (EOC) — the scientific heart of METAXÝ. The thin critical regime between frozen ORDER and pure CHAOS, where structure is stable enough to persist and fluid enough to change — and where computation, life, and maybe mind prefer to live. Langton's lambda (the dial), Rule 110 (proven universal computation, sitting right at the edge), Wolfram's Class IV, and Per Bak's SELF-ORGANIZED CRITICALITY (the sandpile that tunes itself to the critical slope; avalanches of every size — earthquakes, extinctions, neuronal cascades). The direct BRIDGE to the life-science CA spheres + quantum-cellular-automata. ⚠ two-layer: the taxonomy + Rule 110 + SOC are rigorous, but 'life/cognition operate at the edge' is an influential HYPOTHESIS, not settled law (flagged). Langton/Kauffman/Wolfram living cited; Bak (d.2002) minted. LIVE elementary-CA regime sweep (order/edge/chaos). Vellum (no black) + ember + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-interface", "THE INTERFACE · IFC", "#2f8a8a", "metaxy · the surface where two meet · interactive · vellum · 9", "THE INTERFACE (IFC) — METAXÝ as surface: the boundary that both separates and connects (Simone Weil's metaxu — the wall two prisoners tap through). The thinnest, most important part of any system, where inside meets outside without becoming one: the cell MEMBRANE, the skin, the software interface/API, the channel between two minds. Selective permeability (the chooser, not the wall), the protocol (the agreed grammar), the threshold of perception (world->mind). Catalysis on surfaces, meaning in the narrow band — the between is not empty space, it is where everything happens. ⚠ two-layer: each case (membrane/skin/surface/API) is real and concrete; treating them as ONE idea is a unifying METAPHOR offered as analogy, not a claim that biology and software share laws (labeled). Weil (d.1943) minted. LIVE permeable-membrane interactive (toggle the pores). Vellum (no black) + teal + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents."),
   ("the-cyborg", "THE CYBORG · CYB", "#6a6ab8", "metaxy · between organism and machine · interactive · vellum · 9", "THE CYBORG (CYB) — METAXÝ at the human/machine seam: the hybrid that belongs to neither side. Donna Haraway's cyborg (the being of the between, refusing the clean splits) + the ordinary reality already here: PACEMAKERS, cochlear implants, nerve-reading prosthetics, brain-computer interfaces, the extended mind (memory in the device). To merge with a tool is to gain its powers AND inherit its vulnerabilities — extended and exposed in the same motion. Bridges the AI domain (machine half) + life-science (organism half); cousin to organoid-intelligence. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: pacemakers/implants/prosthetics/BCIs are real working medicine helping millions; 'merging with AI' / mind-uploading / full neural integration are speculative or early-stage (separated from the deployed tech); Haraway treated as a philosophical LENS, not a forecast. Haraway LIVING -> cited not minted. LIVE neuron<->circuit morph interactive. Vellum (no black) + steel-violet + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents."),
   ("the-chain-of-thought", "THE CHAIN OF THOUGHT · COT", "#6a4fc0", "niphelektron · pipeline 5 · reasoning as iterated prediction · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE CHAIN OF THOUGHT (COT) — the CAPSTONE of the NIPHELEKTRON inference pipeline (tokenize -> embed -> transform -> predict -> REASON, looped). The 2024-2025 frontier: predict not one token but a long chain of working-out, spend more compute at inference, and a model's answers on hard problems jump. Chain-of-thought prompting (Wei 2022), self-consistency, test-time / inference-time SCALING (a second scaling axis beyond model size), the verifier, adaptive effort. The reasoning-model wave -- OpenAI o1/o3, DeepSeek-R1, Google thinking models, Claude's extended/adaptive thinking -- cited as public fact, not minted. Cross-links the-quorum-engine + the AI domain. STRICTLY two-layer: the gains are real and measured, BUT it is still next-token prediction (not a proof engine), more thinking is not always better, and FAITHFULNESS is an open problem -- a stated chain of thought is not guaranteed to be the true cause of the answer (flagged, load-bearing). LIVE bat-and-ball demo: answer-directly (fast, wrong) vs think-it-through (a streamed scratchpad, right) with a token counter. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-nes", "THE NES · NES", "#3a7a9a", "exereunesis · 8-bit teardown + spec edition · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE NES (NES) — the first sphere of UD0's new 23rd domain EXEREÚNESIS (ἐξερεύνησις, the searching-out): TECHNICAL TEARDOWNS. A full 8-bit Nintendo (1985) hardware teardown + SPEC EDITION. Almost nothing inside: two custom Ricoh chips, 2 KB RAM, a slot. The 2A03 (MOS 6502 core @ 1.79 MHz + the APU on-die), the 2C02 PPU (256x240, 64 sprites / 8 per scanline = the flicker, 54-color palette ~25 on screen), the 5-channel APU, the 2 KB work RAM, and the CARTRIDGE + MAPPER (MMC1/MMC3 bank-switching that kept upgrading the machine for a decade). Plus the 10NES lockout chip + the wear-prone 72-pin connector (the real roots of the blinking power light), the serial controller, NTSC composite out. ⚠ two-layer: chips/clocks/memory-map/sprite limits are documented FACT; the blinking-light + lockout-arms-race LORE is flagged (well-supported version, not the tall tale). Render-not-invent; NO ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; Nintendo/Ricoh + NESdev cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip -> its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + blueprint-slate + quorum-ring favicon. 12 components."),
