   ("psephos", "PSĒPHOS", "#2fc6c0", "The processor — reckoning made substrate. ROOT0's compute-hardware inventions gathered as one: memristive, photonic, plasmonic, ionic, and lattice processors (the 128 → 512 → 4096 build-out), plus the ternary trit-logic they reckon in. The substrate of computation — distinct from LOGISMÓS (the history of computing) and the frontier (the quantum). The pebble that counts. (ψῆφος, psēphos — the counting-stone, the ancient root of 'calculate'; Latin calculus is a pebble too.)"),
